course: dictionary
lesson: 663
title: A word from the north
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one part of the country. «Bairn» is one of them. In Scotland and the north of England, people use it for a child, and sometimes for a baby. «Wee bairn» means a little baby, so the word «wee» (small) is a clue too.
explain: Read the other words in the sentence for clues. «Late night, Rosie?» «Aye, the bairn was greetin' aw night, miss.» Aye means yes, and greetin' means crying. A baby who cries all night is a baby, so bairn must mean baby here.
explain: Be careful with «your bairns». In Scotland it means your children, your own family's kids. Ask yourself who the speaker is talking about, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Words like this show where a speaker comes from and make the talk sound warm and homely. When you are not sure, check a dictionary. Remember that bairn is not used everywhere, so people in other places may say child or kid instead.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Bairn» (Scotland, northern England) means a child or a baby.
fact: «Your bairns» (Scotland) means your children, your own family's kids.
fact: «Wee bairn» means a little baby.
fact: Other Scottish words include «aye» (yes), «ken» (know) and «dinnae» (don't).
exercise: «Late night, Rosie?» «Aye, the bairn was greetin' aw night, miss.» What is the bairn in this sentence? | A teacher | *A baby | A bin lorry | A woolly hat
exercise: Mrs Ross says, «Mind your bairns on the icy path.» What does bairns mean? | Your neighbours | Your parents | *Your children | Your bins
exercise: Where would you most likely hear the word bairn? | Australia | *Scotland and northern England | Canada | Wales only
test: «The bairn gave a big smile when the snow began.» What does bairn mean here? | *A child | A bag of sweets | A snowman | A bin
test: «Are you bringing your bairns to the party?» What does your bairns mean? | Your bins | Your friends from school | *Your own children | Your parents
exam: Dad says, «Wrap the wee bairn up warm, it's baltic out!» Which word in this sentence means freezing cold? | wrap | bairn | *baltic | warm
